WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.432
Hi, I'm Inkwell!

00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:06.617
Mixture-of-experts models store far more weights than any one token uses.

00:00:06.617 --> 00:00:07.378
Here's how.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.269
Swap the one feed-forward network for many experts, and route each token

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:14.477
to just a few.

00:00:18.842 --> 00:00:22.773
The router, one small matrix, gives every expert a score for this token.

00:00:23.193 --> 00:00:24.999
Keep the top eight of sixty-four.

00:00:24.999 --> 00:00:26.504
Only those eight experts run.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:32.638
One shared expert runs on every token, so the routed ones can specialise.

00:00:33.058 --> 00:00:37.158
Outputs are weighted by their gates, summed, and added to the residual stream.

00:00:38.692 --> 00:00:40.963
Every token skips the same share of the model.

00:00:41.383 --> 00:00:44.616
In each of thirty-two layers, fifty-six experts sit idle.

00:00:45.402 --> 00:00:48.041
And each expert holds almost thirty-eight million weights.

00:00:49.226 --> 00:00:54.963
So Hunyuan-A13B stores eighty billion weights but reads under thirteen billion per token.

00:00:56.592 --> 00:01:00.995
Each generation widens the gap: under four stored weights per active one

00:01:00.995 --> 00:01:03.563
in Mixtral, almost twenty-seven in Kimi K3.

00:01:05.192 --> 00:01:09.188
An extra loss evens the load, but its gradient fights the language model.

00:01:09.608 --> 00:01:12.606
DeepSeek-V3 biases the scores for choosing only.

00:01:12.606 --> 00:01:15.603
Busy experts drift down, idle ones up.

00:01:17.192 --> 00:01:21.113
Spread across many GPUs, each MoE layer becomes a round trip.

00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:22.974
Route each token where it lives.

00:01:24.686 --> 00:01:27.079
An all-to-all ships it to its experts' GPUs.

00:01:27.499 --> 00:01:29.471
Each GPU runs its own experts.

00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:32.380
A second all-to-all brings the outputs home.

00:01:33.642 --> 00:01:35.883
Experts add knowledge, not compute per token.

00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:38.765
The bill moves to memory, balance and the network.

00:01:42.192 --> 00:01:44.036
Score, and keep the top few.

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:44.958
Balance the load.

00:01:44.958 --> 00:01:46.494
Ship tokens to their experts.

00:01:46.914 --> 00:01:48.990
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:49.583
I'm Inkwell.

00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:49.879
Bye!
